All Steps performed on raspberry pi 3 B ended up downgrading kernel to 6.6 bc i was not watching the default git links to older version. 
1.) Grab morse micro Kernel that has been patch to have 802.11ah 
git clone --depth 1 --recurse-submodules --shallow-submodules https://github.com/MorseMicro/rpi-linux.git
2.) Your Pi needs the right tools (compilers, parsers, etc.) to translate the C code into machine code. Run this to grab everything you need: 
sudo apt update
sudo apt install git bc bison flex libssl-dev make libc6-dev libncurses5-dev -y
2.) Navigate into morse micro rpi-linux folder:
cd rpi-linux
3.) You need to tell the build system which specific chip architecture it's building for so it enables the correct baseline drivers.  these should be listed inthe Kernel folder
-Raspberry pi 3 or 4: 
make bcm2711_defconfig
4.) Compile the Kernel (takes a while)  $(nproc)  uses all available cpus
make -j$(nproc) Image.gz modules dtbs
if error run (runs on less cores):
make clean
make -j2 Image.gz modules dtbs
5.) Install Kernel moduels
sudo make modules_install

Copy the Kernel and Device Trees:
sudo cp arch/arm64/boot/dts/broadcom/*.dtb /boot/firmware/
sudo cp arch/arm64/boot/dts/overlays/*.dtb* /boot/firmware/overlays/
sudo cp arch/arm64/boot/dts/overlays/README /boot/firmware/overlays/
sudo cp arch/arm64/boot/Image.gz /boot/firmware/kernel8.img

6.) reboot:
sudo reboot
7.) run  uname -a  to see new kernel
8.) install morse_firmware
cd ~
git clone --depth 1 --recurse-submodules --shallow-submodules https://github.com/MorseMicro/morse-firmware.git
cd morse-firmware
sudo make install
9.) Clone and compile mores_driver
cd ~ 
git clone --depth 1 --recurse-submodules --shallow-submodules https://github.com/MorseMicro/morse_driver.git
cd morse_driver
make KERNEL_SRC=/home/nodeuser/rpi-linux CONFIG_WLAN_VENDOR_MORSE=m CONFIG_MORSE_SPI=y CONFIG_MORSE_USER_ACCESS=y CONFIG_MORSE_VENDOR_COMMAND=y CONFIG_MORSE_COUNTRY=US
10.) Load the module
sudo depmod -a
sudo modprobe morse
11.) verify the hardware is recognized:
dmesg | grep -i morse
 dmesg | tail -n 30
dtparam=spi=on dmesg | grep -i morse
dmesg | grep spi
12.) sudo nano /boot/firmware/config.txt # verify 
# Enable the SPI bus dtparam=spi=on # Load the Morse Micro SPI map #dtoverlay=morse-spi
13.) reboot

